WEBVTT

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:10.010
"This is a work of fiction based on research
into the period in which it is set. The people,
organization, laws, and names that appear in it
have no relation to any in the real world."

00:01:40.010 --> 00:01:41.310
"Tokyo City"

00:01:47.770 --> 00:01:49.770
"Tokyo Railway Station"

00:02:03.410 --> 00:02:05.250
Fire!

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:06.660
We'll form a shield!

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:09.210
Don't let a single vamp get through!

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:37.530
Vampire units.

00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:40.530
If you desire the strength of night,

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:44.490
I suggest you join my troupe.

00:02:44.490 --> 00:02:48.580
I am the commander of Special Force Unit 16,

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:51.120
"King of Fools"

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:51.120
Rufus Glenn.

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:52.580
"King of Fools"

00:02:53.380 --> 00:02:55.500
Vampires,

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:58.380
there are two roads open to you.

00:02:58.380 --> 00:02:59.630
One.

00:02:59.630 --> 00:03:06.430
Obey us, Special Forces Unit 16,
and you will receive blood and registrations.

00:03:06.430 --> 00:03:07.520
Two.

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:10.690
Refuse to obey...

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:12.440
...and die.

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:13.360
"Tokyo Station"

00:03:14.770 --> 00:03:15.610
"Nihonbashi"

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:30.120
"Shin Yoshiwara"

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:54.100
"Kannon Temple"

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:55.020
"Asakusa Park"
"Kannon Temple"

00:04:11.410 --> 00:04:13.370
Hey now.

00:04:16.750 --> 00:04:19.250
You're not the star performer.

00:04:26.930 --> 00:04:27.890
Asakusa,

00:04:27.890 --> 00:04:29.810
Nihonbashi, Kyobashi...

00:04:29.810 --> 00:04:31.930
Hongo, Kanda, everywhere...

00:04:31.930 --> 00:04:33.890
The vamps' ranks are swelling.

00:04:33.890 --> 00:04:36.610
We need to rethink our defenses.

00:04:36.610 --> 00:04:41.990
At this rate, the vamps will breach
the Marunouchi safe zone.

00:04:41.990 --> 00:04:46.370
We're doing all we can to maintain
order with the army's finest,

00:04:46.370 --> 00:04:50.620
but handling the vamps
is more than we can manage.

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:52.910
I understand.

00:04:52.910 --> 00:04:58.290
Please let us, Special Forces Unit 16,
see to maintaining order in Marunouchi.

00:05:00.380 --> 00:05:01.800
Thank you very much!

00:05:14.810 --> 00:05:17.600
Burn! Burn!

00:05:17.600 --> 00:05:22.230
Everyone stronger than me should just burn!

00:05:22.230 --> 00:05:24.530
Come on, tonight is the mopping up!

00:05:24.530 --> 00:05:27.610
Hunt down every last one of those nuisances!

00:05:47.010 --> 00:05:50.220
Thank you for all your hard work.

00:05:50.220 --> 00:05:55.310
I, Rufus Glenn, have taken it
upon myself to perfect Code Zero,

00:05:55.310 --> 00:06:00.060
the embodiment of your ideals,
<i>former </i>Ltg. Nakajima.

00:06:00.060 --> 00:06:04.190
They complete their missions
and return without a single casualty.

00:06:04.190 --> 00:06:06.820
An invincible fighting force.

00:06:06.820 --> 00:06:10.490
Of course, none of them are human.

00:06:10.490 --> 00:06:14.370
Now you have no more regrets, right, old man?

00:06:20.290 --> 00:06:22.380
Hurry up and die.

00:06:48.860 --> 00:06:51.820
Now no one is left to stand in my way.

00:06:51.820 --> 00:06:55.290
I am the king of vampires.

00:06:56.500 --> 00:07:00.000
Listen. We shall cross the ocean on that ship.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:02.500
We'll make a kingdom in a new land.

00:07:02.500 --> 00:07:07.550
They're trying to build an invincible army
for the coming world war there!

00:07:07.550 --> 00:07:10.550
Doesn't that sound like fun?

00:07:10.550 --> 00:07:13.220
What about the children?

00:07:13.220 --> 00:07:15.260
Children?

00:07:15.260 --> 00:07:17.470
I'll find you replacements.

00:07:20.310 --> 00:07:23.860
It's my world, after all.

00:07:23.860 --> 00:07:26.230
Whoops.

00:07:26.230 --> 00:07:29.110
It's time for the ambassador's farewell party.

00:07:29.110 --> 00:07:31.200
You wait on the ship.

00:07:45.380 --> 00:07:50.260
I don't feel cold or warmth.

00:07:50.260 --> 00:07:52.590
I'm a vampire.

00:07:59.020 --> 00:08:01.980
Pardon my lateness, Your Excellency.

00:08:01.980 --> 00:08:05.770
Your invincible force is performing admirably.

00:08:05.770 --> 00:08:07.570
You're welcome.

00:08:07.570 --> 00:08:11.950
I promise to do great things
in Your Excellency's country.

00:08:11.950 --> 00:08:15.410
That's reassuring. I have high hopes for you.

00:08:15.410 --> 00:08:17.200
I'm honored, Excellency.

00:08:19.160 --> 00:08:20.580
Oh, my, Rufus!

00:08:20.580 --> 00:08:22.410
Welcome.

00:08:22.410 --> 00:08:26.920
Thank you for inviting me, Madam.

00:08:26.920 --> 00:08:30.840
Rufus, I'm going to pay
my respects to the prime minister.

00:08:30.840 --> 00:08:33.430
May I ask you to escort my wife?

00:08:33.430 --> 00:08:35.090
I'd be honored.

00:08:35.090 --> 00:08:37.180
Please do.

00:08:37.180 --> 00:08:42.060
Now I can look at your lovely face all evening.

00:08:42.060 --> 00:08:46.520
Yes, Rufus Glenn is always at your service.

00:08:57.820 --> 00:09:02.700
How good to see the moon!

00:09:02.700 --> 00:09:06.210
She is like a little piece of money,

00:09:06.210 --> 00:09:09.460
a little silver flower.

00:09:09.460 --> 00:09:12.380
She is cold and chaste.

00:09:12.380 --> 00:09:15.970
I am sure she is a virgin.

00:09:15.970 --> 00:09:20.970
The Lord hath come. The son of man hath come.

00:09:20.970 --> 00:09:23.060
Who was that who cried out?

00:09:23.060 --> 00:09:24.690
--They try, but they can't measure up
to the London original.

00:09:24.690 --> 00:09:28.610
--Ah, the prophet! He of whom
the Tetrarch is afraid?
--They try, but they can't measure up
to the London original.

00:09:28.610 --> 00:09:29.360
--Ah, the prophet! He of whom
the Tetrarch is afraid?
--It's lovely.

00:09:29.360 --> 00:09:30.730
--It is thy mouth...
--It's lovely.

00:09:33.240 --> 00:09:36.570
I will give thee all that is mine,

00:09:36.570 --> 00:09:40.450
save only the life of one man.

00:09:40.450 --> 00:09:45.410
Thy voice is as music to mine ear.

00:09:45.410 --> 00:09:50.290
Speak again...

00:09:51.920 --> 00:09:53.760
...Danny Boy.

00:09:57.220 --> 00:09:59.010
Defrott.

00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:06.190
I guess this is it for Code Zero.

00:10:06.190 --> 00:10:08.650
I was rather fond of it.

00:10:08.650 --> 00:10:12.820
The <i>torii </i>corridor was set dressing
to draw the enemy's eye.

00:10:12.820 --> 00:10:16.240
Of course, I always planned
to erase all evidence,

00:10:16.240 --> 00:10:19.490
but they saved me the trouble.

00:10:19.490 --> 00:10:21.410
Takeuchi.

00:10:21.410 --> 00:10:24.370
This is where I leave you.

00:10:24.370 --> 00:10:26.830
I'll miss you.

00:10:26.830 --> 00:10:28.870
I'm not happy about it.

00:10:28.870 --> 00:10:30.540
Is it Ayame?

00:10:30.540 --> 00:10:32.960
I was the one who left her loose.

00:10:32.960 --> 00:10:35.300
I have to deal with it.

00:10:35.300 --> 00:10:40.970
In that case, I'll just have
to have Kurusu do his best.

00:10:40.970 --> 00:10:43.560
Would you give that to him?

00:10:43.560 --> 00:10:45.890
All right.

00:10:45.890 --> 00:10:47.480
So long.

00:10:50.190 --> 00:10:53.480
That was awfully abrupt for a comrade.

00:10:53.480 --> 00:10:56.690
I'm sure we'll meet again someday if we live.

00:10:56.690 --> 00:11:00.200
Suwa and I both have long lives ahead of us.

00:11:00.200 --> 00:11:01.950
Takeuchi!

00:11:01.950 --> 00:11:04.120
Takeuchi, Takeuchi, let's play Mikan!

00:11:04.120 --> 00:11:06.200
All right.

00:11:08.830 --> 00:11:10.790
Mikan.

00:11:10.790 --> 00:11:12.040
Fine, fine.

00:11:12.040 --> 00:11:14.960
Let's head back to Asakusa.

00:11:14.960 --> 00:11:17.670
Hey now, look where you're going.

00:11:21.260 --> 00:11:22.550
Here you go!

00:11:22.550 --> 00:11:23.680
Thank you.

00:11:23.680 --> 00:11:24.510
Here!

00:11:24.510 --> 00:11:26.390
Thank you for everything.

00:11:26.390 --> 00:11:27.220
Here.

00:11:27.220 --> 00:11:28.480
Sorry about this.

00:11:28.480 --> 00:11:29.690
Not at all.

00:11:29.690 --> 00:11:32.060
Okay, I still need to deliver to...

00:11:32.060 --> 00:11:33.730
Recovered already?

00:11:33.730 --> 00:11:36.610
Yup! I'm all better now.

00:11:36.610 --> 00:11:42.820
I panicked when you were
brought here at death's door.

00:11:42.820 --> 00:11:46.870
It's thanks to all the vampires here.

00:11:46.870 --> 00:11:51.790
I was surprised at first,
but they're all good people.

00:11:51.790 --> 00:11:58.880
I've started wishing I could help them
all the time like you do, Mr. Tenmanya.

00:11:58.880 --> 00:11:59.880
I see.

00:11:59.880 --> 00:12:00.800
Oh, right.

00:12:00.800 --> 00:12:02.760
Have you seen Shutaro?

00:12:02.760 --> 00:12:06.310
I believe Mr. Kurusu is out front.

00:12:06.310 --> 00:12:07.930
Thanks a million!

00:12:13.810 --> 00:12:15.360
How's Mikan?

00:12:15.360 --> 00:12:16.820
They're working hard.

00:12:16.820 --> 00:12:19.230
Stop, Yoh! It's my turn!

00:12:19.230 --> 00:12:21.950
They've both adjusted quite well.

00:12:21.950 --> 00:12:27.200
We're able to grasp the vampire unit's
movements better now as well.

00:12:27.200 --> 00:12:29.330
I think it's time.

00:12:29.330 --> 00:12:30.950
I'm prepared.

00:12:30.950 --> 00:12:32.790
I'll let everyone know.

00:12:32.790 --> 00:12:34.750
Please do.

00:12:34.750 --> 00:12:38.250
Now, we should get started as well.

00:12:38.250 --> 00:12:40.260
This is Takeuchi.

00:12:41.800 --> 00:12:43.340
Understood.

00:12:43.340 --> 00:12:44.720
Oh, found you!

00:12:47.470 --> 00:12:50.470
You haven't eaten yet, right, Shutaro?

00:12:50.470 --> 00:12:52.390
This is for you!

00:12:52.390 --> 00:12:54.650
It's vampire food, right?

00:12:56.440 --> 00:12:58.770
I... don't need it.

00:12:58.770 --> 00:13:02.110
But it's your meal.

00:13:02.110 --> 00:13:04.820
I've still never drunk blood.

00:13:04.820 --> 00:13:07.910
That's not very vampire-like.

00:13:07.910 --> 00:13:10.370
I really am a vampire.

00:13:10.370 --> 00:13:12.830
I'm weak to sunlight, for one.

00:13:12.830 --> 00:13:15.920
Defrott was scared of it, too.

00:13:15.920 --> 00:13:18.250
How about crosses and stuff?

00:13:18.250 --> 00:13:21.210
I'm fine with those.

00:13:21.210 --> 00:13:25.840
But the smells of garlic, rotten fish,
and <i>natto </i>are hard to deal with.

00:13:25.840 --> 00:13:27.970
That's good to know.

00:13:27.970 --> 00:13:29.470
What do you mean?

00:13:33.180 --> 00:13:36.980
So, is it true you don't age?

00:13:38.400 --> 00:13:40.070
Yeah.

00:13:40.070 --> 00:13:42.650
It's kind of hard to believe.

00:13:42.650 --> 00:13:45.900
Hey, show me something vampire-y!

00:13:48.660 --> 00:13:50.030
Like this?

00:13:52.200 --> 00:13:53.660
Believe me now?

00:13:55.540 --> 00:13:56.750
Yup.

00:14:01.040 --> 00:14:02.250
Again!

00:14:02.250 --> 00:14:03.090
Huh?

00:14:03.090 --> 00:14:05.760
Do that disappearing thing again!

00:14:09.640 --> 00:14:10.890
Okay.

00:14:14.600 --> 00:14:21.190
Shutaro, where are you?

00:14:21.190 --> 00:14:22.650
Everyone left.

00:14:22.650 --> 00:14:23.610
Huh?

00:14:23.610 --> 00:14:25.900
For Tokyo Station.

00:14:25.900 --> 00:14:28.240
They won't come back here.

00:14:29.950 --> 00:14:32.200
Won't you follow?

00:14:32.200 --> 00:14:35.700
I knew.

00:14:35.700 --> 00:14:41.080
Shutaro is a vampire, and I'm human.

00:14:41.080 --> 00:14:44.590
We can't be together forever.

00:14:44.590 --> 00:14:48.300
Even if I chase him, I couldn't catch up.

00:14:50.340 --> 00:14:53.220
True, vampires are different from us.

00:14:53.220 --> 00:14:58.190
Their injuries heal instantly,
and they don't age.

00:14:58.190 --> 00:15:02.270
But they question why they're alive.

00:15:02.270 --> 00:15:04.780
On moonlit nights like this,

00:15:04.780 --> 00:15:10.360
they laugh, they cry, and just when
they seem to make mistakes,

00:15:10.360 --> 00:15:13.280
they do the right thing.

00:15:13.280 --> 00:15:16.450
In that sense, vampires and humans are the same.

00:15:18.540 --> 00:15:22.130
But if you have something
to tell him, you should hurry.

00:15:22.130 --> 00:15:26.920
Unlike theirs, our time is limited.

00:15:28.720 --> 00:15:30.930
--Huh?
--I'm returning this!

00:15:34.600 --> 00:15:35.930
Head clerk.

00:15:35.930 --> 00:15:37.350
I'm here, sir.

00:15:37.350 --> 00:15:39.520
The streets aren't safe at night.

00:15:39.520 --> 00:15:40.640
Yes, sir.

00:15:44.310 --> 00:15:45.940
I hope she makes it.

00:15:47.480 --> 00:15:49.490
How...

00:15:49.490 --> 00:15:51.410
...is he alive?

00:15:58.950 --> 00:16:02.500
Damn it, vampire units, what are you doing?

00:16:02.500 --> 00:16:05.210
You're supposed to be standing guard!

00:16:05.210 --> 00:16:06.210
Assemble!

00:16:06.210 --> 00:16:07.670
Assemble here!

00:16:07.670 --> 00:16:09.340
I'm right here!

00:16:11.590 --> 00:16:12.890
Damn!

00:16:19.430 --> 00:16:21.730
Tokyo Station?

00:16:21.730 --> 00:16:23.520
Vampire units...

00:16:23.520 --> 00:16:25.270
Where are they?!

00:16:28.820 --> 00:16:31.150
You're late!

00:16:36.830 --> 00:16:37.910
You're...

00:16:37.910 --> 00:16:39.580
Code Zero?!

00:16:39.580 --> 00:16:41.500
Didn't you die in that fire?!

00:16:41.500 --> 00:16:43.330
I finally found you.

00:16:43.330 --> 00:16:44.960
You found me?!

00:16:44.960 --> 00:16:46.840
Are you working for Defrott, too?

00:16:46.840 --> 00:16:48.750
Is that it?!

00:16:48.750 --> 00:16:50.880
Wh-What?

00:16:52.090 --> 00:16:53.630
Stay back.

00:16:53.630 --> 00:16:54.800
Fall back.

00:16:55.970 --> 00:16:57.220
Now,

00:16:57.220 --> 00:17:00.680
where is the scariest "it" right now?

00:17:00.680 --> 00:17:01.680
Here!

00:17:01.680 --> 00:17:03.600
I see.

00:17:03.600 --> 00:17:04.730
I was first!

00:17:04.730 --> 00:17:06.230
--Me.
--Me!

00:17:06.230 --> 00:17:08.520
--Me.
--It was me, Yoh!

00:17:08.520 --> 00:17:10.230
--No, me.
--It was me!

00:17:10.230 --> 00:17:11.610
Kurusu,

00:17:11.610 --> 00:17:14.150
the rest is up to you.

00:17:14.150 --> 00:17:16.110
You there, civilian,

00:17:16.110 --> 00:17:18.990
evacuate as far away from here as you can.

00:17:18.990 --> 00:17:21.500
"Civilian"? Me?!

00:17:21.500 --> 00:17:23.790
Vampire units! Kill him!

00:17:23.790 --> 00:17:24.790
Hurry u--

00:17:46.520 --> 00:17:47.770
I'm...

00:17:49.060 --> 00:17:53.820
I'm the king of vampires.

00:17:53.820 --> 00:17:56.570
I'm... the king.

00:18:03.080 --> 00:18:04.790
You're all useless!

00:18:04.790 --> 00:18:06.750
I'm the king of this world!

00:18:06.750 --> 00:18:08.290
The king of vampires!

00:18:08.290 --> 00:18:10.210
I! Am! King!

00:18:10.210 --> 00:18:12.050
Mr. Rufus.

00:18:12.050 --> 00:18:13.800
What?! De--

00:18:15.220 --> 00:18:18.300
Let me show you to your room.

00:18:34.900 --> 00:18:37.150
This is my room?

00:18:37.150 --> 00:18:39.450
How long until we reach the USA?

00:18:39.450 --> 00:18:42.950
Roughly two weeks via Honolulu.

00:18:42.950 --> 00:18:48.290
Don't grin at Rufus Glenn
like that. It's disgusting.

00:18:48.290 --> 00:18:50.040
I shall rest.

00:18:50.040 --> 00:18:53.960
Don't knock on this door even if the world ends.

00:18:53.960 --> 00:18:56.220
Enjoy your voyage.

00:19:04.640 --> 00:19:06.930
Have you woken from your dream?

00:19:10.520 --> 00:19:14.530
I'll prepare a different dream for you.

00:19:21.490 --> 00:19:25.290
I had a funny dream earlier.

00:19:25.290 --> 00:19:29.920
I wasn't a vampire. Me.

00:19:29.920 --> 00:19:32.540
Ridiculous, don't you think?

00:19:32.540 --> 00:19:36.300
Good night forever, Danny Boy.

00:19:41.050 --> 00:19:42.430
Suwa.

00:19:42.430 --> 00:19:45.810
Are you here to kill me? I'm a traitor.

00:19:45.810 --> 00:19:47.310
Go ahead. Kill me.

00:19:47.310 --> 00:19:50.060
I can't survive on my own anyway.

00:19:54.480 --> 00:19:56.900
Dying, huh?

00:19:57.900 --> 00:20:00.030
It's almost sunrise.

00:20:16.340 --> 00:20:21.090
No!

00:20:21.090 --> 00:20:23.010
Why would you do this?

00:20:24.640 --> 00:20:27.970
This is what dying is.

00:20:28.970 --> 00:20:32.980
If you wanted to die, you'd be dead already.

00:20:32.980 --> 00:20:36.190
But you're still alive.

00:20:36.190 --> 00:20:39.780
Even though nothing makes sense to you,

00:20:39.780 --> 00:20:42.910
you still want to live, right?

00:20:42.910 --> 00:20:45.870
I was created by him.

00:20:45.870 --> 00:20:48.700
But I've had enough!

00:20:48.700 --> 00:20:52.290
Enough of corrupted blood
running through my veins!

00:20:54.460 --> 00:20:59.300
There's a lot of different
vampires' blood in my veins.

00:20:59.300 --> 00:21:03.470
If we're just talking about blood, mine's worse.

00:21:03.470 --> 00:21:06.180
Still, I...

00:21:06.180 --> 00:21:09.310
We haven't lived this long because of blood.

00:21:09.310 --> 00:21:11.850
Our hearts kept us alive.

00:21:11.850 --> 00:21:15.100
Don't you want to believe that?

00:21:15.100 --> 00:21:18.570
If you can't go on living on your own...

00:21:20.230 --> 00:21:23.280
...then I'll stick with you.

00:21:23.280 --> 00:21:25.450
What?

00:21:25.450 --> 00:21:29.280
If you're worried about
those two, they're fine now.

00:21:42.970 --> 00:21:47.550
Want to visit the "new world"
together for a change of pace?

00:23:42.000 --> 00:23:46.960
"Frailty, Thy Name Is..."
